Mmm, you know how much I talk about this sambal.

58
00:13:40,716 --> 00:13:44,216
Indonesia has a wide variety of sambal from different regions.

59
00:13:44,216 --> 00:13:49,216
Sambal roa is a Manado specialty, and it is mainly made from chili...

60
00:13:49,216 --> 00:13:52,216
...and smoked ballyhoo fish.

61
00:13:52,216 --> 00:13:55,216
Mari kita coba.
Let's try it.

62
00:13:55,216 --> 00:13:58,716
Enak... Yummy!
Delicious... Yummy!

63
00:14:04,216 --> 00:14:07,216
Next, we're gonna take some Tahu Lada Garam.

64
00:14:07,216 --> 00:14:11,716
Mmm, salt and pepper tofu, yummy!

65
00:14:12,216 --> 00:14:16,716
Ooh, it's salt-and-pepper fried tofu complete with Indonesian aromatics.

66
00:14:16,716 --> 00:14:18,716
Let's have a taste!

67
00:14:21,716 --> 00:14:24,716
Hmm, this is like buttery flavor. I like it so much.
Hmm, this has like a buttery flavor. I like it so much.

68
00:14:25,216 --> 00:14:28,216
And this one is a Sundanese specialty called karedok.

69
00:14:28,216 --> 00:14:32,216
It's a traditional salad that uses a rich peanut sauce.

70
00:14:32,216 --> 00:14:41,216
Mmm, it has green eggplants, cucumbers, lemon basil, long beans, as well as bean sprouts.

71
00:14:41,716 --> 00:14:43,716
So fresh!

72
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:46,716
Segar banget!
So refreshing!

73
00:14:47,216 --> 00:14:49,216
Next up, we're going to go eat some fish!

74
