840
00:59:15,788 --> 00:59:18,288
ジャンプしながら喋ったことはないよ（笑）
I've never tried yapping while balling, okay?

841
00:59:18,288 --> 00:59:22,288
新しいスキルを身につけるのに遅すぎることはないよ！
Never too late to pick up a new skill.

842
00:59:22,288 --> 00:59:24,288
履歴書に書けるね（笑）
Put it on your resume.

843
00:59:24,288 --> 00:59:30,788
それと前と同じように、2人ずつ競い合います。なので、パートナーとしっかり会話を続けてね！
Yeah, and just like before, two people will compete at a time. So make sure you keep chatting with your partner while you race.

844
00:59:30,788 --> 00:59:33,788
対戦相手だけどパートナーってことね
Opponent, partner, same thing.

845
00:59:33,788 --> 00:59:36,788
おしゃべりし続けないといけないんだね
Alright, the yapping has to...

846
00:59:36,788 --> 00:59:39,788
大丈夫？ちょっとトリックを試そうとしたんだけど（笑）
Are you okay? I tried doing a trick, I'm sorry.

847
00:59:39,788 --> 00:59:43,288
ごめんごめん（笑）
Sorry, sorry.

848
00:59:43,288 --> 00:59:47,288
そして2つ目のルールは、折り返し地点を過ぎたら、相手の邪魔をしてもOKです！
Okay, and the second rule is, after you pass that point, you can try to mess with your opponent.

849
00:59:47,288 --> 00:59:50,788
だから、こょこよしたり、何でもしていいよ！
So if you want to tickle your opponent...

850
00:59:50,788 --> 00:59:54,288
え、ちょっと！やめて！（笑）
Wait! Stop!

851
00:59:54,288 --> 00:59:57,288
私はそんなことしないから安心してね！
Hey, I'm not going to do that to you.

852
00:59:57,288 --> 01:00:00,188
基本的にはそんな感じです！
Yeah, basically like that.

853
01:00:01,296 --> 01:00:02,696
We tried this during rehearsal,

854
01:00:02,696 --> 01:00:03,596
well, I tried,

855
01:00:03,596 --> 01:00:05,896
and I guess it's going to be, you know...

856
01:00:05,896 --> 01:00:08,696
It's kind of tiring, so it's your choice basically.

857
01:00:08,696 --> 01:00:09,796
You can just, like,

858
01:00:09,796 --> 01:00:11,496
focus on racing, or you know,

859
01:00:11,496 --> 01:00:14,796
if you have... you're a little bit more, what's it, mischievous, you want to tickle,

860
01:00:14,796 --> 01:00:16,196
you want to tickle your opponent?

861
01:00:16,196 --> 01:00:16,796
Tickle?

862
01:00:16,796 --> 01:00:18,096
Yeah, you want to,

863
01:00:18,096 --> 01:00:19,796
yeah, you want to lift them up and kiss them, that's fine too.

864
01:00:19,796 --> 01:00:21,096
Are you too ticklish?

865
01:00:21,096 --> 01:00:22,196
I'm not ticklish.

866
01:00:22,196 --> 01:00:23,096
I'm not.

867
01:00:23,096 --> 01:00:25,796
I think she might be ticklish. No, I'm not ticklish at all.

868
01:00:25,796 --> 01:00:29,296
Reine, use it to your advantage. Never let your opponent know your weakness.

869
01:00:29,296 --> 01:00:33,696
Tickle tickle tickle tickle. No no no.

870
01:00:33,696 --> 01:00:34,496
But anyway,

871
01:00:34,496 --> 01:00:36,196
all right, everybody, let's get into position.

872
01:00:36,196 --> 01:00:37,796
Calli and Kiara.

873
01:00:37,796 --> 01:00:39,496
Oh boy, I'm first again.

874
01:00:39,496 --> 01:00:40,396
That's fine.

875
01:00:40,396 --> 01:00:41,696
You're going to be facing...

876
01:00:41,696 --> 01:00:42,796
You're already getting started.

877
01:00:42,796 --> 01:00:44,296
Don't make it too hard for yourself.

878
01:00:44,296 --> 01:00:45,496
Yeah.

879
01:00:45,496 --> 01:00:47,296
You make it harder for yourself.

880
01:00:47,296 --> 01:00:48,996
Wait, what's our topic?

881
01:00:48,996 --> 01:00:51,296
Wait wait wait, hold on hold on. I'm going to go here first.

882
01:00:51,296 --> 01:00:52,596
Oh!

883
01:00:52,596 --> 01:00:54,196
Which topic?

884
01:00:54,196 --> 01:00:55,296
Okay,

885
01:00:55,296 --> 01:00:57,796
your topic is...

886
01:00:57,796 --> 01:01:01,296
Things I love about my cat!

887
01:01:01,296 --> 01:01:03,396
Oh, easy! Right? 猫自慢。
Oh, easy! Right? Bragging about cats.

888
01:01:03,396 --> 01:01:04,796
That's a pretty easy one.

889
01:01:04,796 --> 01:01:07,896
You guys both have adorable cats at home, so go ahead and brag as much as you want.

890
01:01:07,896 --> 01:01:09,796
Okay.

891
01:01:09,796 --> 01:01:11,796
Yes.

892
01:01:11,796 --> 01:01:14,796
That might actually help me forget that I'm tired.

893
01:01:14,796 --> 01:01:16,796
Oh yeah, cats take that all away.

894
01:01:16,796 --> 01:01:19,296
So fluffy, okay.

895
01:01:19,296 --> 01:01:21,796
What about... can we talk about that cat over there?

896
01:01:21,796 --> 01:01:23,296
No!

897
01:01:23,296 --> 01:01:25,296
Focus on your game.

898
01:01:25,296 --> 01:01:28,096
That's a secret agent disguised as a cat.

899
01:01:28,096 --> 01:01:31,296
Or a cat disguised as a secret agent.

900
01:01:31,296 --> 01:01:33,396
Okay.

901
01:01:33,396 --> 01:01:34,496
Are you guys ready?

902
01:01:34,496 --> 01:01:35,796
Yeah, ready as I'll ever be.

903
01:01:35,796 --> 01:01:37,796
All right, on your marks.

904
01:01:37,796 --> 01:01:42,096
Three, two, one, go!

905
01:01:42,096 --> 01:01:44,296
Chuchu is so fluffy and cute. She has a bobble...

906
01:01:44,296 --> 01:01:46,596
black stripe down the back of her... What are you doing?

907
01:01:46,596 --> 01:01:49,796
Her tail is so fluffy and long.

908
01:01:49,796 --> 01:01:53,296
No, what are you doing?

909
01:01:53,296 --> 01:01:55,296
Wait, oh my god!

910
01:01:55,296 --> 01:01:57,496
Should we increase the distance?

911
01:01:57,496 --> 01:02:01,596
Should we make it a little further? Do we still have to finish it?

912
01:02:01,596 --> 01:02:05,496
Well, tell me a little bit about your cats, Kiara.

913
01:02:05,496 --> 01:02:08,396
Yes, so currently,

914
01:02:08,396 --> 01:02:11,296
I'm not with my cats so that makes me really sad.

915
01:02:11,296 --> 01:02:13,396
But my cat caretakers

916
01:02:13,396 --> 01:02:15,896
are sending me videos of them and they're sleeping like on the towels

917
01:02:15,896 --> 01:02:19,796
even though I said "Don't sleep on the towels because the towels are not supposed to have cat hair all over."

918
01:02:19,796 --> 01:02:23,296
But it's okay, I forgive them. I just buy new towels so there are cat towels and there are human towels.

919
01:02:23,296 --> 01:02:26,096
That's a good idea to separate them like that.

920
01:02:26,096 --> 01:02:29,296
Oh, she's finished!

921
01:02:29,296 --> 01:02:33,296
Yay! That was so good.

922
01:02:33,296 --> 01:02:35,796
Nice job. Good job.

923
01:02:35,796 --> 01:02:38,296
That was so good. Oh my.

924
01:02:38,296 --> 01:02:42,796
Well done, well done. I respect the legwork. That was intense.

925
01:02:42,796 --> 01:02:45,496
I mean, this is... I actually do this during my training anyway.

926
01:02:45,496 --> 01:02:46,596
Oh!

927
01:02:46,596 --> 01:02:49,796
Yeah, hold the ball between my legs and jump. So I kind of had an unfair advantage.

928
01:02:49,796 --> 01:02:52,796
Oh, so you're... okay, you have that skill.

929
01:02:52,796 --> 01:02:54,896
I do this every muscle training session.

930
01:02:54,896 --> 01:02:56,496
You trained with balling.

931
01:02:56,496 --> 01:02:58,496
Okay.

932
01:02:58,496 --> 01:03:01,296
Well, let's announce your times, girls, please.

933
01:03:01,296 --> 01:03:04,096
Let's go, let's go, let's go.

934
01:03:04,096 --> 01:03:05,796
Yay!

935
01:03:05,796 --> 01:03:06,696
頑張れ、頑張れ！
Go for it, go for it!

936
01:03:06,696 --> 01:03:08,796
Well, I won, but who won?

937
01:03:08,796 --> 01:03:12,496
Oh, that was a close one.

938
01:03:12,496 --> 01:03:16,796
It was very, very close.

939
01:03:16,796 --> 01:03:18,796
So, okay, set up, please.

940
01:03:18,796 --> 01:03:20,796
All right.

941
01:03:20,796 --> 01:03:21,796
So,

942
01:03:21,796 --> 01:03:24,796
it was... it's close.

943
01:03:24,796 --> 01:03:26,796
Can you say my time first?

944
01:03:26,796 --> 01:03:28,796
Okay, your time first. Okay, let's see.

945
01:03:28,796 --> 01:03:34,496
Kiara, your time was 46.5 seconds!

946
01:03:34,496 --> 01:03:40,296
Oh yeah! That's pretty fast.

947
01:03:40,296 --> 01:03:42,796
Yeah!

948
01:03:42,796 --> 01:03:45,796
That's a crazy dance move. She showed us how to throw it down.

949
01:03:45,796 --> 01:03:48,496
Okay, now Calli...

950
01:03:48,496 --> 01:03:50,496
It was a close one.

951
01:03:50,496 --> 01:03:52,496
Yeah, that was a really close one.

952
01:03:52,496 --> 01:03:57,296
Your time was 10.5 seconds!

953
01:03:57,296 --> 01:04:03,296
Oh my god!

954
01:04:03,296 --> 01:04:05,796
I could've been a little faster, I guess.

955
01:04:05,796 --> 01:04:11,796
This is me on a slow day, actually. Go Kiara!

956
01:04:11,796 --> 01:04:14,796
Yeah, I need to work on my feelings and...

957
01:04:14,796 --> 01:04:16,396
Feelings?

958
01:04:16,396 --> 01:04:19,296
Oh, your feelings. How are you feeling?

959
01:04:19,296 --> 01:04:21,096
I had an unfair advantage.

960
01:04:21,096 --> 01:04:23,096
I just wish I was a baller.

961
01:04:23,096 --> 01:04:24,796
Oh, first you got to be a little bit taller.

962
01:04:24,796 --> 01:04:27,796
By a 6'4 Impala.

963
01:04:27,796 --> 01:04:29,296
And then we'll talk.

964
01:04:29,296 --> 01:04:32,296
Well, I hope that your match will be a little bit closer.

965
01:04:32,296 --> 01:04:34,296
Oh, ganbare.
Oh, good luck.

966
01:04:34,296 --> 01:04:36,296
What match? Our match?

967
01:04:36,296 --> 01:04:37,796
Ganbatte.
Do your best.

968
01:04:37,796 --> 01:04:39,496
Ganba, ganba. You're up.
Do your best, do your best. You're up.

969
01:04:39,496 --> 01:04:40,896
Take your ball.

970
01:04:40,896 --> 01:04:42,496
Go get your ball. Go get your ball.

971
01:04:42,496 --> 01:04:45,496
Sorry, I left my ball.

972
01:04:45,496 --> 01:04:48,296
Don't forget your balls. Get my ball. Don't forget.

973
01:04:48,296 --> 01:04:50,296
Hey, can we make our balls meet?

974
01:04:50,296 --> 01:04:51,296
What?

975
01:04:51,296 --> 01:04:53,796
Hi, nice to meet you. This is my ball.

976
01:04:53,796 --> 01:04:55,296
Nice to meet you too.

977
01:04:55,296 --> 01:04:57,096
Oh, we just met.

978
01:04:57,096 --> 01:04:58,796
We just met.

979
01:04:58,796 --> 01:05:00,296
Do your balls know each other?

980
01:05:00,304 --> 01:05:01,604
Not yet, not yet!

981
01:05:01,604 --> 01:05:03,104
After this race...

982
01:05:03,104 --> 01:05:04,504
...we'll get to know each other now.

983
01:05:04,504 --> 01:05:08,804
Alrighty. Well then, it looks like I'm going to be tanto for this match.
Alrighty. Well then, it looks like I'm going to be in charge of this match.

984
01:05:08,804 --> 01:05:10,304
Ayo.

985
01:05:10,304 --> 01:05:12,104
So... here is your topic.

986
01:05:12,104 --> 01:05:14,604
Okay? Compliment each other in Japanese!

987
01:05:14,604 --> 01:05:16,404
ええー！？
What!?

988
01:05:16,404 --> 01:05:19,804
No English, no Indonesian allowed.

989
01:05:19,804 --> 01:05:24,104
This is a good challenge for somebody, or two people, who speak three languages!

990
01:05:24,104 --> 01:05:26,804
That's right.

991
01:05:26,804 --> 01:05:28,304
Kiara also speaks three languages.

992
01:05:28,304 --> 01:05:30,304
So you'll have no excuse.

993
01:05:30,304 --> 01:05:31,804
Compliment each other in German.

994
01:05:31,804 --> 01:05:34,804
German?

995
01:05:34,804 --> 01:05:37,304
Guten Morgen!
Good morning!

996
01:05:37,304 --> 01:05:39,804
Danke schön! Danke schön!
Thank you very much! Thank you very much!

997
01:05:39,804 --> 01:05:41,804
Okay. Are you ready?

998
01:05:41,804 --> 01:05:45,804
And on your marks, get set, go!

999
01:05:45,804 --> 01:05:48,304
ゼタ、可愛い！先輩、可愛い！
Zeta, you're cute! Senpai, you're cute!

1000
01:05:48,304 --> 01:05:50,304
ゼタ、髪が綺麗！
Zeta, your hair is beautiful!

1001
01:05:50,304 --> 01:05:52,804
先輩、足長い！
Senpai, your legs are long!

1002
01:05:52,804 --> 01:05:54,804
デートに行かない？
Do you want to go on a date?

1003
01:05:54,804 --> 01:05:57,804
デートに行こう！チューチューチュー！
Let's go on a date! Chu chu chu!

1004
01:05:57,804 --> 01:06:00,804
Wait, wait.

1005
01:06:00,804 --> 01:06:03,804
I think so. I'm pretty sure I heard some compliments.

1006
01:06:03,804 --> 01:06:07,304
It was a little hard to hear what they were saying, but they were definitely complimenting each other.

1007
01:06:07,304 --> 01:06:09,304
What were you saying to each other?

1008
01:06:09,304 --> 01:06:13,304
Um, I was saying "Zeta kawaii," "ashi nagai," and then...
Um, I was saying "Zeta is cute," "long legs," and then...

1009
01:06:13,304 --> 01:06:17,804
..."your hair is pretty," and then "let's go on a date sometime," and then I said "chu chu chu."
..."your hair is pretty," and then "let's go on a date sometime," and then I said "kiss, kiss, kiss."

1010
01:06:17,804 --> 01:06:20,804
Those are compliments. Yeah, those are compliments.

1011
01:06:20,804 --> 01:06:22,104
What did you say to her?

1012
01:06:22,104 --> 01:06:25,104
I said, "Wow, 君は素晴らしい!"
I said, "Wow, you are amazing!"

1013
01:06:25,104 --> 01:06:28,304
And, "拳が強い!"
And, "Your fists are strong!"

1014
01:06:28,304 --> 01:06:30,804
And, "根性!"
And, "Grit!"

1015
01:06:30,804 --> 01:06:33,104
And, "てて!"
And, "Hand in hand!"

1016
01:06:33,104 --> 01:06:36,304
Yeah, those are compliments. That was successful, then. Good job, team.

1017
01:06:36,304 --> 01:06:38,804
And we got the times ready? Maybe too?

1018
01:06:38,804 --> 01:06:42,804
Good job. Let's check out the times.

1019
01:06:42,804 --> 01:06:45,304
We both know each other now.

1020
01:06:45,304 --> 01:06:48,304
Let's meet! Let's meet!

1021
01:06:48,304 --> 01:06:51,304
Alrighty, fine, fine.

1022
01:06:51,304 --> 01:06:54,304
I want my ball to hang out with you guys too.

1023
01:06:54,304 --> 01:06:58,304
Oh, wow. We only just met, but this is kind of fun.

1024
01:06:58,304 --> 01:07:02,304
I don't know.

1025
01:07:02,304 --> 01:07:08,804
Do we have the times? Let's check them out. We probably have them now. I think I could tell who won, though.

1026
01:07:08,804 --> 01:07:11,504
Ah, got it. You saw it.

1027
01:07:11,504 --> 01:07:13,804
It was close!

1028
01:07:13,804 --> 01:07:17,304
It was definitely closer than ours.

1029
01:07:17,304 --> 01:07:19,304
Just like earlier, it was close.

1030
01:07:19,304 --> 01:07:22,804
Okay, we got it. The times... do you want to say them?

1031
01:07:22,804 --> 01:07:26,804
Now, Reine, your time was... 12 seconds!

1032
01:07:26,804 --> 01:07:29,804
Yay!

1033
01:07:29,804 --> 01:07:33,804
And Zeta...

1034
01:07:33,804 --> 01:07:36,804
大丈夫？ 大丈夫、大丈夫。
Are you okay? Yeah, I'm okay.

1035
01:07:36,804 --> 01:07:40,304
Zeta, your time was... 14 seconds!

1036
01:07:40,304 --> 01:07:42,804
Wow!

1037
01:07:42,804 --> 01:07:46,304
Good job! Any number with the number four in it is a good number.

1038
01:07:46,304 --> 01:07:51,804
It is a good number. So, the winner of your match was...

1039
01:07:51,804 --> 01:07:53,304
...Reine!

1040
01:07:53,304 --> 01:07:55,304
Yay!

1041
01:07:55,304 --> 01:07:58,304
How do you feel?

1042
01:07:58,304 --> 01:08:01,304
Yeah, I feel great. Energized.

1043
01:08:01,304 --> 01:08:03,304
Ready for more exercise?

1044
01:08:03,304 --> 01:08:05,804
Yeah, great.

1045
01:08:05,804 --> 01:08:07,804
It is rigged. She is the birthday girl, of course she would win.

1046
01:08:07,804 --> 01:08:10,804
Everyone, you all did an amazing job.

1047
01:08:10,804 --> 01:08:15,304
We finished both games, so we're going to total up everyone's times and announce the winner.

1048
01:08:15,304 --> 01:08:20,304
Yes, find out who has the shortest total time.

1049
01:08:20,304 --> 01:08:24,304
It's hot here in Indonesia today, isn't it?

1050
01:08:24,304 --> 01:08:26,804
Alright, take a breath, take a breath.

1051
01:08:26,804 --> 01:08:29,304
CPR, CPR, CPR please!

1052
01:08:29,304 --> 01:08:32,304
Kiara, you do it! Do you do it, you do the CPR.

1053
01:08:32,304 --> 01:08:35,304
I'm dying, somebody CPR please.

1054
01:08:35,304 --> 01:08:38,304
Kiara will do it.

1055
01:08:38,304 --> 01:08:41,804
I'm alive! Are you okay?

1056
01:08:41,804 --> 01:08:46,804
事故、事故！ 事故、事故！
Emergency, emergency! Emergency, emergency!

1057
01:08:46,804 --> 01:08:49,304
She lives! I'm alive!

1058
01:08:49,304 --> 01:08:52,804
お疲れ。お疲れ、you're alive. Congrats on being alive.
Good job. Good job, you're alive. Congrats on being alive.

1059
01:08:52,804 --> 01:08:57,304
Do we have the results yet?

1060
01:08:57,304 --> 01:09:00,304
Wait, wait, while we're waiting on the results, here's my sick trick.

1061
01:09:00,304 --> 01:09:03,304
Calli, catch! Okay, I'm ready.

1062
01:09:03,304 --> 01:09:05,804
Are you ready to catch? Yeah.

1063
01:09:05,804 --> 01:09:08,804
Well, it was a little low.

1064
01:09:08,804 --> 01:09:13,304
Again, again.

1065
01:09:13,304 --> 01:09:15,304
Three, two, one...

1066
01:09:15,304 --> 01:09:18,304
Nice!

1067
01:09:18,304 --> 01:09:21,304
Let's go, TakaMori! TakaMori ball masters!

1068
01:09:21,304 --> 01:09:25,304
TakaMori knows ball.

1069
01:09:25,304 --> 01:09:28,304
Wow, we're ballin'.

1070
01:09:28,304 --> 01:09:31,304
That was awesome, that was a sick trick. We should become like a football club.

1071
01:09:31,304 --> 01:09:36,804
Our team! Oh, results are in!

1072
01:09:36,804 --> 01:09:40,304
We got them, we got them. The results are in, and let's announce the winner, okay?

1073
01:09:40,304 --> 01:09:43,304
And let's start with... the fourth place! Drumroll please!

1074
01:09:43,304 --> 01:09:48,304
*drumroll*

1075
01:09:48,304 --> 01:09:51,804
Takanashi Kiara!

1076
01:09:51,804 --> 01:09:55,304
Four is the best number! Last place but I mean, first place in...

1077
01:10:00,312 --> 01:10:01,612
...in your hearts, right?

1078
01:10:01,612 --> 01:10:03,512
Yes! So true, so true.

1079
01:10:03,612 --> 01:10:05,412
Fourth place is first from the bottom!

1080
01:10:05,412 --> 01:10:06,612
あ、すごい！
Ah, that's amazing!

1081
01:10:06,612 --> 01:10:08,012
I'm so goi!
I'm so amazing!

1082
01:10:08,012 --> 01:10:09,412
Also, number one balloon.
Also, the number one balloon.

1083
01:10:09,412 --> 01:10:11,012
Number one baller.

1084
01:10:11,012 --> 01:10:13,112
You see how well she knows that ball.

1085
01:10:13,112 --> 01:10:14,212
Yeah, see?

1086
01:10:14,212 --> 01:10:15,812
Whoa! Whoa!

1087
01:10:15,812 --> 01:10:17,812
Okay, and then...

1088
01:10:17,812 --> 01:10:21,312
The third place is our very own beloved house cat!

1089
01:10:21,312 --> 01:10:24,312
Vestia Zeta!

1090
01:10:24,312 --> 01:10:26,612
Our beloved house cat, secret agent!

1091
01:10:26,612 --> 01:10:28,812
Yay, I'm third place!

1092
01:10:28,812 --> 01:10:30,812
Okay, hands please, hands please!

1093
01:10:30,812 --> 01:10:32,512
Yeah, she's so cute.

1094
01:10:32,512 --> 01:10:33,712
Okay, good girl!

1095
01:10:33,712 --> 01:10:35,112
Congratulations!

1096
01:10:35,112 --> 01:10:37,312
That's not how you dog-sit though.

1097
01:10:37,312 --> 01:10:39,012
Cat, dog, same thing, same thing.

1098
01:10:39,012 --> 01:10:41,312
Not the same animal, not the same animal.

1099
01:10:41,312 --> 01:10:42,812
They're adjacent, whatever.

1100
01:10:42,812 --> 01:10:44,512
Okay, and in second place...

1101
01:10:44,512 --> 01:10:47,712
...just missing out on the win...

1102
01:10:47,712 --> 01:10:50,812
It's Pavolia Reine!

1103
01:10:50,812 --> 01:10:54,312
Oh my god! Yay, girl! I know her!

1104
01:10:54,312 --> 01:10:57,312
Wait, Calli, you didn't let her win on her birthday?

1105
01:11:00,012 --> 01:11:01,812
Oh, should I... Wait, what? Should I have done that?

1106
01:11:01,812 --> 01:11:04,812
Is that, like, a manners thing?

1107
01:11:04,812 --> 01:11:07,812
Oh god, sorry, sorry!

1108
01:11:07,812 --> 01:11:11,312
No, no, I prepared something for the winner, so that's okay.

1109
01:11:11,312 --> 01:11:15,812
And that means our champion with the fastest time, Mr. Ball...

1110
01:11:15,812 --> 01:11:18,312
Mori Calliope!

1111
01:11:18,312 --> 01:11:21,312
Mr. Ball? Please don't hurt me.

1112
01:11:21,312 --> 01:11:24,312
Congratulations! - Thank you!

1113
01:11:24,312 --> 01:11:28,312
Thank you, oh my gosh! I appreciate it, I've been training.

1114
01:11:28,312 --> 01:11:31,312
So, Mori...

1115
01:11:31,312 --> 01:11:35,812
...who got the fastest time, has earned a very special trophy.

1116
01:11:35,812 --> 01:11:38,812
Thank you! - Ta-da-da-da-da!

1117
01:11:38,812 --> 01:11:41,112
Oh, trophy! I have to... can I touch my ball too?

1118
01:11:41,112 --> 01:11:43,112
Yes, this is a very special trophy for today!

1119
01:11:43,112 --> 01:11:45,812
Whoa, I like it!

1120
01:11:45,812 --> 01:11:50,812
Thank you! Thank you so much! Thank you!

1121
01:11:50,812 --> 01:11:54,812
Anyways, any comments? Any, you know, winner interview?

1122
01:11:54,812 --> 01:12:00,812
Um, this is really fun! I had such a great time enjoying Indonesia!

1123
01:12:00,812 --> 01:12:06,812
But more than anything, I'm glad we all got to have lots of fun on your very special day. Reine, thank you for inviting us...

1124
01:12:06,812 --> 01:12:12,812
...and sharing with us some of the games that, you know, you used to like to play. It was just a really good time, so thank you!

1125
01:12:12,812 --> 01:12:18,812
No, thank you so much, Calli, and thank you, Kiara and Zeta, for participating!

1126
01:12:18,812 --> 01:12:22,812
And that's all for the games. Thank you so much for playing with me, everyone!

1127
01:12:22,812 --> 01:12:26,812
Yay! Thank you!

1128
01:12:26,812 --> 01:12:30,812
And coming up next in the stream, I have a very, very special surprise!

1129
01:12:30,812 --> 01:12:34,812
A brand new song performance!

1130
01:12:34,812 --> 01:12:38,812
Whoa! New song, new song! New song, new song!

1131
01:12:38,812 --> 01:12:42,312
But before we get there, I want to show you...

1132
01:12:42,312 --> 01:12:48,312
...uh, the teaser video for the new song and introduce some merch!

1133
01:12:48,312 --> 01:12:52,312
So don't go anywhere and stay with us until the very end.

1134
01:12:52,312 --> 01:12:54,312
We will! Yay!

1135
01:12:54,312 --> 01:12:57,312
All right, now let's take a look at the teaser video for the new song!

1136
01:12:57,312 --> 01:13:00,312
Here you go!

1137
01:13:19,312 --> 01:13:22,312
Pavolia Reine New Original Song
Endless Blue
2026.09.09 24:00 RELEASE
[Pavolia Reine New Original Song: Endless Blue]
[Released on 2026.09.09 at 24:00]

1138
01:13:25,812 --> 01:13:29,812
How did you like the teaser video?

1139
01:13:29,812 --> 01:13:32,812
Yeah! Yeah! What are they doing?

1140
01:13:32,812 --> 01:13:36,312
You guys are so suspicious!

1141
01:13:36,312 --> 01:13:41,312
So, well, this new song is, you know my very first original song, Gate Open: START?

1142
01:13:41,312 --> 01:13:44,312
Yes! Yes!

1143
01:13:44,312 --> 01:13:49,312
So if Gate Open: START is the opening of an anime...

1144
01:13:49,312 --> 01:13:54,312
...this is kind of, you know, a little bit more mellow vibe, maybe like a second season opening of Gate Open: START.

1145
01:13:54,312 --> 01:13:57,312
I love that, yeah!

1146
01:13:57,312 --> 01:14:00,312
Reine anime when? Let's go!

1147
01:14:00,312 --> 01:14:03,312
Yay! I'd watch it!

1148
01:14:03,312 --> 01:14:06,312
Second season, omedetou! - Omedetou!
Second season, congratulations! - Congratulations!

1149
01:14:06,312 --> 01:14:11,312
Well, as I mentioned earlier, I'll be performing it later, so please look forward to it!

1150
01:14:11,312 --> 01:14:15,812
And now, before I perform the new song, I'd like to have my guests here...

1151
01:14:15,812 --> 01:14:20,812
...my beautiful, beautiful guests, help me introduce this year's birthday merch!

1152
01:14:20,812 --> 01:14:24,312
All right, everyone, get over here! We won't let you down!

1153
01:14:24,312 --> 01:14:27,812
Buy! Buy! Buy! Buy! Buy! Get out your wallet!

1154
01:14:27,812 --> 01:14:30,312
Ta-da!

1155
01:14:30,312 --> 01:14:35,312
Okay, first up, 'Take me with U' Acrylic Diorama Stand!

1156
01:14:35,312 --> 01:14:41,312
Featuring a beautiful illustration by Enji-sensei of me enjoying me-time with a beautiful view!

1157
01:14:41,312 --> 01:14:46,812
Whenever you go to a restaurant, please take me with you!

1158
01:14:46,812 --> 01:14:48,812
What are you guys doing?

1159
01:14:48,812 --> 01:14:52,312
Take your oshikatsu pictures! Don't forget oshikatsu!
Take your fan support pictures! Don't forget fan support!

1160
01:14:52,312 --> 01:14:56,312
Next...

1161
01:15:02,320 --> 01:15:03,820
おいおい、キアラ？
Oi oi, Kiara?

1162
01:15:03,820 --> 01:15:06,120
待って待って！あなた、これに出番あるの？
Wait, wait! Do you have a part in this?

1163
01:15:06,120 --> 01:15:08,820
うん、仕事があるんだよ！
Yes, I have a job to do.

1164
01:15:08,820 --> 01:15:12,520
2つ目のアイテムを紹介します！トラベルタオルー！
I will introduce the second item: the Travel Towel!

1165
01:15:12,520 --> 01:15:14,320
トラベルタオルー！
Travel Towel!

1166
01:15:14,320 --> 01:15:18,820
名前に騙されないでね。これはとっても万能なタオルで、
Don't let the name fool you, this is a super versatile towel...

1167
01:15:18,820 --> 01:15:24,320
旅行だけでなく、普段の生活でも使えます。脇を拭いて、脇を拭いて！
that you can use not only for traveling, but also in your everyday life. Wipe your armpits, wipe your armpits!

1168
01:15:24,320 --> 01:15:28,820
例えば、次のフェスでも大活躍すること間違いなし！
It sure will come in handy at the next fest too, for example!

1169
01:15:28,820 --> 01:15:32,820
タオル！タオル！タオル！タオル！
Towel! Towel! Towel! Towel!

1170
01:15:34,520 --> 01:15:37,120
次、次、次、次。
And next, next, next, next.

1171
01:15:37,120 --> 01:15:42,820
そして3つ目のアイテムは、じゃじゃーん！ミーアヤムボウル！
And the third item is... ta-da! Mie Ayam Bowl!

1172
01:15:42,820 --> 01:15:45,520
イェーイ！
Yay!

1173
01:15:45,520 --> 01:15:50,320
ミーアヤム！アヤム！ミーアヤム！美味しい、美味しい！
Mie Ayam! Ayam! Mie Ayam! Delicious, delicious!

1174
01:15:50,320 --> 01:15:55,320
名前が示す通り、このボウルはミーアヤムを食べるのにぴったりですが、ラーメンや、
As the name suggests, this bowl is perfect for eating Mie Ayam, but it's also great for ramen,

1175
01:15:55,320 --> 01:15:59,520
スープ、その他あらゆる料理にも最適です。
soup, and all kinds of other dishes.

1176
01:15:59,520 --> 01:16:05,820
だから、たくさん使ってもらえると思います。何にでも使えますよ！
So, I'm sure you'll get lots of use for it. You can use it for anything!

1177
01:16:05,820 --> 01:16:08,820
キャットフードを入れてもいいよね！
You can even put cat food into it!

1178
01:16:08,820 --> 01:16:11,820
帽子としても使えるよ！
You can even use it as a hat!

1179
01:16:11,820 --> 01:16:14,320
何でもありだね！アヤム、アヤム...
Whatever works!

1180
01:16:14,320 --> 01:16:19,320
そう、このボウルで美味しい食事をたくさん楽しんでね！
Yeah, I hope this bowl helps you enjoy lots of tasty meals!

1181
01:16:19,320 --> 01:16:24,320
素晴らしい！そして最後になりますが、4つ目のアイテム…冗談、最後じゃないよ、4つ目のアイテム！
Very nice! And last but certainly not least, the fourth item—just kidding, it's not last, it's the fourth item!

1182
01:16:24,320 --> 01:16:27,820
死神だから4番に配属されたんだけどね。
But I was assigned number four because I am a Shinigami.

1183
01:16:27,820 --> 01:16:32,320
4つ目のアイテムは、愛らしい旅のパートナー、ぬいぐるみキーホルダー！
The fourth item is... the lovely travel partner plushie keychain!

1184
01:16:32,320 --> 01:16:36,820
すべての旅行や冒険に持っていくのにぴったりのサイズです。
It is the perfect size to bring on all your trips and your adventures.

1185
01:16:36,820 --> 01:16:42,820
この衣装を着た可愛い小さなレイネをどこにでも連れて行って、一緒にたくさん楽しんでくださいね！
Take this adorable little Reine in her costume with you wherever you go and have lots of fun together!

1186
01:16:42,820 --> 01:16:45,820
イェーイ！素晴らしい！
Yay! Spectacular!

1187
01:16:45,820 --> 01:16:50,320
イェーイ！そして今回は、特別なシチュエーションボイスもあります。
Yay! And this time, I also have a special situational voice:

1188
01:16:50,320 --> 01:16:53,320
「不気味な旅のパートナー」！
"Spooky travel partner"!

1189
01:16:53,320 --> 01:16:57,320
3カ国語で収録された怖い話が入っています！
It includes scary stories recorded in three languages!

1190
01:16:57,320 --> 01:17:01,320
すごい！マルチリンガル！超怖い！
Great! Multilingual! So scary!

1191
01:17:01,320 --> 01:17:06,320
英語、インドネシア語、日本語…今回はミックスボイスはありません、ごめんね、ミックス言語のボイスはありません。
English, Indonesian, Japanese... No mixed voice this time, sorry, no mixed language voice.

1192
01:17:06,320 --> 01:17:11,820
そしてもちろん、フルセットには限定のポストカード特典が付いてきます！
And of course, the full set comes with an exclusive postcard bonus!

1193
01:17:11,820 --> 01:17:12,820
お見逃しなく！
Don't miss out!

1194
01:17:12,820 --> 01:17:19,320
手書きサイン入りのポストカードも数量限定でご用意していますので、このチャンスをお見逃しなく！
We also have a limited number of postcards with my handwritten signature, so make sure you don't miss out on this chance!

1195
01:17:19,320 --> 01:17:21,320
レイネのサインが欲しい！
I want Reine's autograph!

1196
01:17:21,320 --> 01:17:23,320
そう、レイネのサインが欲しい！
Yes, I want Reine's autograph!

1197
01:17:23,320 --> 01:17:25,320
レイネのサインが欲しい！
I want Reine's autograph!

1198
01:17:25,320 --> 01:17:30,320
いやいや、私、私を先にして！超高速で買うから！どいてどいて。
Hey, no, me! Me first! I'm going to buy real fast! Get out of my way.

1199
01:17:30,320 --> 01:17:32,320
私のライフィーのスピードに勝てる？
Can you beat my lifey speed?

1200
01:17:32,320 --> 01:17:35,320
絶対無理！でも、みんな最前列で会おうね、行こう。
Definitely not! But I'll see you guys in the pit, let's go.

1201
01:17:35,320 --> 01:17:38,320
レイネのサインのために戦うんだ。みんな準備しておけよ。
Fighting for Reine's signature. All you guys better be ready.

1202
01:17:38,320 --> 01:17:40,320
もう十分に戦ったんじゃないの？
Didn't we already fight enough?

1203
01:17:40,320 --> 01:17:42,320
いや、今度はファンと戦いたいんだ。そう、次はファンの番だ。
Well, I want to fight the fans now. Yes, it's their turn now.

1204
01:17:42,320 --> 01:17:44,320
次は君たちだ！
You guys are next!

1205
01:17:44,320 --> 01:17:48,820
ということで、グッズ紹介は以上になります！
And that wraps up our merch introduction!

1206
01:17:48,820 --> 01:17:50,820
よし、下がって、下がって、下がって！
Okay, move back, back, back!

1207
01:17:50,820 --> 01:17:52,820
下がって、下がって、下がって…どこに下がるの？
Back back back... Back to where?

1208
01:17:52,820 --> 01:17:54,320
自分がどこにいたか忘れちゃった！
I forgot where I was!

1209
01:17:54,320 --> 01:17:56,320
自分がどこにいたか分からないよ！
I don't know where I was!

1210
01:17:56,320 --> 01:17:58,320
ここ、多分ここでいいと思う。みんな、ふぅ！
Here, maybe here is fine. Okay guys, whew!

1211
01:17:58,320 --> 01:18:02,820
今年の誕生日会は本当に楽しかったです！
This year's birthday celebration was so much fun!

1212
01:18:02,820 --> 01:18:09,320
2つの異なるロケ撮影に行けて、みんなと一緒に過ごせて、たくさんの素晴らしい思い出ができました。
I got to go to two different location shoots, spend time with everyone, and make so many great memories.

1213
01:18:09,320 --> 01:18:14,820
だから、私の誕生日をこんなに楽しくしてくれて、本当に、本当にありがとうございました！
So, thank you, thank you so much again for making my birthday so fun!

1214
01:18:14,820 --> 01:18:18,320
どういたしまして！おいで、おいで！
You're welcome! Bring it in, bring it in!

1215
01:18:18,320 --> 01:18:23,820
レイネが1歳年上になったね。
Reine is one year older.

1216
01:18:23,820 --> 01:18:26,320
1歳年上になりました！
I'm one year older!

1217
01:18:26,320 --> 01:18:29,320
私に近づいたこと、おめでとう。
Congrats on getting closer to me.

1218
01:18:29,320 --> 01:18:31,320
髪の毛が白くなってきてるよ。
Your hair is turning grey.

1219
01:18:31,320 --> 01:18:35,320
あなたのもね！
Ours is too!

1220
01:18:35,320 --> 01:18:39,320
そして、あっという間に配信の最後の部分に達してしまいました。
And now, before we know it, we've reached the final part of the stream.

1221
01:18:39,320 --> 01:18:44,320
新曲のパフォーマンスの時間です！
And it is time for the new song performance!

1222
01:18:44,320 --> 01:18:49,320
ちょっと待って、みんなに見せたいものがあるの。ちょっと取ってくるね。
Wait, hold on, I gotta show you something, I'm going to get something.

1223
01:18:49,320 --> 01:18:52,320
何を取ってくるの？どこに行くの？
What are you gonna get? Where is she going?

1224
01:18:52,320 --> 01:18:54,820
もしかしてあれかな？
Is it what I think it is?

1225
01:18:54,820 --> 01:18:57,820
私の愛しい、愛しいベイビー！
My beautiful, beautiful baby!

1226
01:18:57,820 --> 01:19:02,320
わぁ！何それ！ベース！レイネのベースだ！
Woah! Oh my god! Bass! It's the Reine bass!

1227
01:19:02,320 --> 01:19:06,320
ステッカーを見て！このステッカー、みんな見覚えある？
Look at the stickers! Do you guys recognize these stickers?

1228
01:19:06,320 --> 01:19:08,820
おおー！
Ooh!

1229
01:19:08,820 --> 01:19:16,320
よし、これには本当に、本当に一生懸命取り組んだので、みんなに楽しんでもらえると嬉しいです。
All right, I worked really, really hard on this so I hope you all can enjoy it.

1230
01:19:16,320 --> 01:19:20,820
それじゃあ、みんな新曲のタイトルを一緒に言ってくれる？
All right, can everyone say the title of the new song together with me?

1231
01:19:20,820 --> 01:19:22,320
よし、いこう！
Okay, let's go!

1232
01:19:22,320 --> 01:19:23,820
せーの…
Se-no...

1233
01:19:23,820 --> 01:19:29,320
エンドレス・ブルー！
Endless Blue!

1234
01:19:52,320 --> 01:19:56,320
Endless Blue
作詞：藤原優樹 作曲・編曲：長谷川大介
Endless Blue
Lyrics: Yuki Fujiwara | Composition & Arrangement: Daisuke Hasegawa

1235
01:20:01,328 --> 01:20:06,428
[インストルメンタル]
[Instrumental Intro]

1236
01:20:06,428 --> 01:20:11,528
飾り付けた言葉でなんて 本当の鼓動隠してたんだ
I was hiding my true heartbeat behind decorative words...

1237
01:20:11,528 --> 01:20:16,828
折りたたんだ羽は 見えない空に焦がれてた
My folded wings were longing for an invisible sky.

1238
01:20:16,828 --> 01:20:21,628
パズルなら壊してしまった 散らばる欠片 バラバラ
If it were a puzzle, I would have broken it, scattered pieces fell apart.

1239
01:20:21,628 --> 01:20:26,328
誰かに似た色じゃ意味がない わかってるから
Because I know a color that looks like someone else's is meaningless.

1240
01:20:26,328 --> 01:20:31,128
旅立ちはあの青空のせいだ
My departure is all because of that blue sky.

1241
01:20:31,128 --> 01:20:37,828
誤魔化せない憧れに気づいたから
Because I realized an admiration that cannot be deceived.

1242
01:20:37,828 --> 01:20:42,328
どうしようもない衝動に駆られて
Driven by an uncontrollable urge,

1243
01:20:42,328 --> 01:20:47,128
動き出したストーリーの先には
at the end of the story that has begun to move,

1244
01:20:47,128 --> 01:20:52,328
不安も もろい思いさえも 染めてゆく
it dyes even my anxiety and fragile feelings.

1245
01:20:52,328 --> 01:20:58,828
想像より眩しい空が広がってるはずでしょう<
A sky brighter than imagined must be spreading out, right?

1246
01:20:58,828 --> 01:21:01,328
扉を開け行こう
Let's open the door and go.

1247
01:21:01,328 --> 01:21:10,328
[インストルメンタル]
[Instrumental Break]

1248
01:21:10,328 --> 01:21:15,128
有耶無耶に進む昨日も 叫び傷む今日も
Yesterday, which moved forward vaguely, and today, which screams and hurts,

1249
01:21:15,128 --> 01:21:20,328
今更なんて言って 願いの色は薄れていった
saying "it's too late now," the color of my wish faded away.

1250
01:21:20,328 --> 01:21:25,228
痛みなら飲み干してしまおう また乗り越えてみせるよ
If it's pain, I'll drink it all up; I'll show you I can overcome it again.

1251
01:21:25,228 --> 01:21:30,228
私でいることにためらう弱さはもういらない
I no longer need the weakness of hesitating to be myself.

1252
01:21:30,228 --> 01:21:35,128
広げた羽は飾りじゃないよ
My spread wings are not just for show.

1253
01:21:35,128 --> 01:21:42,828
鮮やかな夢を纏おう その覚悟がここにあるから
Let's wear a vivid dream, because that determination is right here.

1254
01:21:42,828 --> 01:22:01,828
[インストルメンタル]
[Instrumental Break]

1255
01:22:01,828 --> 01:22:06,428
幻想の夜重ねて
Piling up night after night of illusions,

1256
01:22:06,428 --> 01:22:11,128
漂うように歩いていたよ
I was walking as if drifting along.

1257
01:22:11,128 --> 01:22:16,228
途方もなく遠くて 挫けそうになっても
Even if it's endlessly far and I'm about to give up,

1258
01:22:16,228 --> 01:22:23,828
この声は羽ばたけるその時を待っていたんだ
this voice of mine was waiting for the moment to take flight.

1259
01:22:23,828 --> 01:22:28,828
もう一度叫んでみるよ
I'll try to scream once more!

1260
01:22:28,828 --> 01:22:33,328
終わりなんてない旅を続けたくて
Wanting to continue a journey with no end,

1261
01:22:33,328 --> 01:22:38,328
進んでいくストーリーの向こうへと
I move forward, beyond the story.

1262
01:22:38,328 --> 01:22:43,128
この声で果てない空を渡っていく
With this voice, I'll cross the endless sky.

1263
01:22:43,128 --> 01:22:47,328
まだ知らない遥かな青に
To the far-off blue that I don't know yet,

1264
01:22:47,328 --> 01:22:50,328
胸を膨らませて
with my heart full of expectation,

1265
01:22:50,328 --> 01:22:55,228
無限の明日がきっと待っているから
because a limitless tomorrow is surely waiting.

1266
01:22:55,228 --> 01:22:57,828
扉を開け行こう
Let's open the door and go.

1267
01:22:57,828 --> 01:23:23,428
[インストルメンタル]
[Instrumental Outro]

1268
01:25:05,336 --> 01:25:36,336
